@startuml deployment-diagram
!include ../_style.iuml
title Cupcake Store · Deployment diagram (production)
left to right direction

node "Customer / staff device" as Dev {
  artifact "Browser\n(mobile-first web app)\nlocalStorage: cart, active orders" as Browser
  artifact "HTTP client (curl)\nstaff pickup API, no UI" as Staff
}

cloud "Vercel (project: cupcake-app, region gru1)" as V {
  node "Routing (vercel.json)\n/api/* → api · /* → web" as Router
  node "Service web\nNext.js 16 (apps/web)\nServer + Client Components" as Web
  node "Service api\nVercel Function (Fluid compute)\nFastify 5 (apps/api)" as Api
}

cloud "Neon (sa-east-1)" as N {
  database "PostgreSQL 16\nbranch main (production)\nbranch preview (PR previews)\npooled + direct URLs" as Db
}

node "GitHub" as GH {
  artifact "Repository\n(monorepo)" as Repo
  artifact "GitHub Actions\nci.yml: lint, types, tests\n(Postgres service)\nrelease.yml: migrate, seed,\nsmoke check, tag" as CI
}

Browser --> Router : HTTPS\npages, /api/* (same origin)
Staff --> Router : HTTPS\nPATCH /api/orders/{code}/pickup\nBearer staff token
Router --> Web
Router --> Api
Web --> Api : server fetch for SSR\n(API_URL service binding)
Api --> Db : TLS · Prisma 7 + pg adapter\n(pooled URL)
CI ..> Db : prisma migrate deploy + seed\n(direct URL, on release)
Repo --> CI : push / PR / manual release
Repo ..> V : Git integration\n(preview per PR, production on main)
@enduml
